     "up": {"title":"Element or trend? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>Nine descriptions taken closely from the notes. Several elements sound alike, so read each one carefully before matching.</p>","pairs":[{"l":"Companies or teams that develop, package and finance digital media products at scale","r":"Producers"},{"l":"Individuals who generate original content, often independently","r":"Creators"},{"l":"Digital environments where content is hosted and discovered","r":"Platforms"},{"l":"Entities that deliver content through networks, CDNs and ISPs","r":"Distributors"},{"l":"Cloud services, hosting providers and telecoms that keep everything running","r":"Infrastructure providers"},{"l":"Businesses and organisations that commission websites, campaigns and branded video","r":"Clients"},{"l":"Gateways, subscription billing and monetisation tools that enable commerce","r":"Payment systems"},{"l":"Creators building sustainable businesses directly with audiences, bypassing gatekeepers","r":"Creator economy growth"},{"l":"A change that has redefined audience attention and content formats on phones","r":"Short-form and vertical video"}],"win":"Well matched. You can tell close elements apart and separate the elements from the trends acting on them."}
