     "up": {"title":"Ripples in the ecosystem (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","intro":"<p>You run digital media for the Trinidad music label Steelpan Sound. Four changes hit in one season, and the obvious answer is not always the best one. Weigh each decision against the whole ecosystem.</p>","nodes":{"start":{"text":"<p><b>Change 1: the algorithm.</b> A platform now pushes short vertical clips, and your long horizontal videos reach fewer new viewers. Your analytics also show that 60% of full-video watch time comes from loyal diaspora fans in New York and Toronto watching on large screens.</p>","choices":[{"t":"Make vertical clips for discovery, keep releasing full videos for the loyal audience, and link the clips to the full releases.","to":"n2","fb":"Good. You adapted to the platform without abandoning the audience your own data shows is most valuable."},{"t":"Keep posting exactly as before; the algorithm will change back.","to":"bad1","fb":"Platforms rarely reverse such shifts. Ignoring a ripple leaves you behind."},{"t":"Switch completely to vertical clips and stop making full videos.","to":"bad1","fb":"You followed the platform but ignored your analytics, losing the diaspora viewers who watch longest."}]},"n2":{"text":"<p><b>Change 2: the regulator.</b> A new data protection rule requires clear consent for marketing emails. Your list of 4,000 fans was built from ticket sales, and nobody was asked for consent.</p>","choices":[{"t":"Keep using the list, because the rule surely applies only to new contacts.","to":"bad2","fb":"Assuming the rule does not apply is a serious risk; contacts collected without consent are exactly what it targets."},{"t":"Delete the whole list and do nothing else.","to":"ok1","fb":"Compliant, but you lose contact with every fan when you could have invited them to opt in again."},{"t":"Stop emailing the old list, and invite fans to re-subscribe through a clear consent form promoted on social media and at shows.","to":"n3","fb":"Correct. You comply with the rule and rebuild a list of fans who actually want your emails."}]},"n3":{"text":"<p><b>Change 3: the advertiser.</b> A rum brand will sponsor your content if you prove who watches. Your channel includes a popular series filmed with a youth steelpan school, and rules restrict alcohol advertising aimed at children.</p>","choices":[{"t":"Share the analytics and accept the sponsorship across every video, including the youth series.","to":"bad3","fb":"Placing alcohol sponsorship on content for children breaks advertising rules and damages trust."},{"t":"Send screenshots of a few positive comments instead of data.","to":"bad4","fb":"Advertisers pay for measurable attention. Comments are not evidence of reach."},{"t":"Share analytics on age, location and watch time, and offer the sponsorship only on the over-18 Carnival series, with age restrictions switched on.","to":"n4","fb":"Excellent. Evidence for the advertiser, and the regulator's rules respected for young viewers."}]},"n4":{"text":"<p><b>Change 4: the infrastructure.</b> Your new single is due out at 6 p.m. At noon, a fibre cable fault takes most of Trinidad offline for the rest of the day.</p>","choices":[{"t":"Postpone the release by a month to be safe.","to":"ok2","fb":"Safe, but you lose the promotion already paid for and the momentum with fans."},{"t":"Ask your partner studio in Barbados to upload at 6 p.m. so diaspora fans get it on time, and tell local fans on your radio partner that it will be waiting when they reconnect.","to":"good","fb":"Smart. You used another node in your network to route around the outage and kept every audience informed."}]},"good":{"text":"<p><b>Grade One season!</b> You balanced platform reach with your own analytics, complied with the regulator, matched the sponsor to the right audience and routed around an infrastructure failure. Every decision showed that the elements of the ecosystem are interdependent.</p>","end":"good"},"ok1":{"text":"<p><b>Safe but costly.</b> You avoided a fine, but your next show sells fewer tickets because no fans were invited back. Lesson: compliance and audience-building can go together.</p>","end":"ok"},"ok2":{"text":"<p><b>Safe but slow.</b> The single eventually does well, but a rival release takes the attention you had built. Lesson: a resilient plan uses other parts of the network when one part fails.</p>","end":"ok"},"bad1":{"text":"<p><b>Reach and loyalty both suffer.</b> Either new viewers never find you, or your most loyal fans drift away. Lesson: respond to the platform, but let your own analytics guide the response.</p>","end":"bad"},"bad2":{"text":"<p><b>Complaint filed.</b> A fan reports the label to the regulator and the story spreads online. Lesson: a regulator's rule ripples straight into your marketing.</p>","end":"bad"},"bad3":{"text":"<p><b>Sponsorship withdrawn.</b> Parents complain, the regulator investigates and the brand pulls out. Lesson: advertisers, audiences and regulators are linked.</p>","end":"bad"},"bad4":{"text":"<p><b>Deal lost.</b> The brand chooses a rival band that supplied audience data. Lesson: analytics systems connect creators and advertisers with evidence.</p>","end":"bad"}}}
