     "up": {"title":"Follow the dependencies (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>This time a failure travels <b>backwards</b> along the dependency chain. A hurricane strikes Dominica. Put the ripple in order, starting with the first link to break and ending with the creators.</p>","blocks":[{"t":"A hurricane damages the undersea-cable landing station and mobile towers in Dominica."},{"t":"People on the island can no longer get online to watch or share videos."},{"t":"Platforms record far fewer views and impressions from Dominica."},{"t":"With no audience to measure, advertisers pause campaigns aimed at the island."},{"t":"Platforms' advertising income from the Dominican market drops."},{"t":"Dominican creators' share of ad revenue falls, and some postpone new productions."}],"win":"Correct. Infrastructure failed, so audiences lost access, so audience data dried up, so advertisers withdrew, so platforms lost income, so creators were paid less. Every link depends on the one beneath it."}
