     "up": {"title":"Tap the professional behaviours (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","intro":"<p>Kemar's busier week as a freelance editor in Montego Bay. Some choices look helpful but break a professional standard, and some look small but matter a great deal.</p>","q":"Tap EVERY action that shows good professional practice (portfolio, client communication, ethics, continuous learning).","lines":["1. Confirmed the brief, the deadline and the number of revisions in writing before starting.","2. Put the client's advert in his portfolio the day before the client launched it.","3. Warned the client two days ahead that delivery would be one day late, and offered a preview.","4. Used a royalty-free track and saved a copy of the licence in the project folder.","5. Reused footage he shot for one client in a job for that client's competitor.","6. Waited until the next morning to reply calmly to a rude email from the client.","7. Told his followers that a camera review was paid for by the manufacturer.","8. Let an AI tool rewrite the client's script and delivered it as entirely his own work.","9. Stored the client's customer list on a public shared drive so the whole team could reach it."],"correct":[0,2,3,5,6],"win":"Correct. Written confirmation, early warning about a delay, keeping licences, a calm reply and disclosing a paid review are all professional. Publishing before launch, reusing a client's footage, hiding AI use and exposing client data are not.","miss":"Look again. Ask of each action: does it respect the client's permission and property, keep communication clear and timely, and stay honest with the audience?"}
