     "up": {"title":"The digital divide (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","q":"A Ministry of Education will move all CAPE revision materials online and can fund ONE measure to reduce the digital divide. A student survey finds: 92% own a smartphone, 41% have home broadband, 18% own a laptop, and the average data plan is 2 GB a month. Which measure is BEST supported by the data?","options":[{"t":"Arrange with mobile providers for the revision portal to use no data, and design every resource to work well on a phone.","ok":true,"fb":"Correct. It builds on the device most students own and removes the data-cost barrier that limits them."},{"t":"Keep printing every resource, so nothing changes for students.","fb":"This avoids the divide rather than reducing it, and students lose the benefits of online materials."},{"t":"Run training for teachers on the new website.","fb":"Useful, but it does nothing for the students' access gap that the survey reveals."},{"t":"Give every student a laptop.","fb":"It is very costly and solves the device gap, but most students already have phones; the larger gap shown is connectivity and data."}]}
