     "up": {"title":"Evaluate the funding option (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","q":"Pitons Play in St. Lucia has a prototype mobile game, no income and plans to expand across the region. It has four offers: (A) a USD 50,000 bank loan at 10%; (B) an angel investor offering USD 50,000 for 20% plus mentoring; (C) a venture capital firm offering USD 50,000 for 45%, a board seat and a target of one million downloads in a year; (D) a USD 15,000 regional grant for games featuring Caribbean heritage. The founders want expertise but also want to keep control. Which plan is MOST suitable?","options":[{"t":"Take the venture capital offer, because it brings the most expertise.","fb":"For the same sum as the angel, the founders would give up 45%, a board seat and accept an aggressive target. They would lose the control they want to keep."},{"t":"Apply for the heritage grant, and take the angel's offer for the rest: no repayments, mentoring, and the founders keep 80% of the company.","ok":true,"fb":"Correct. The grant is free money that fits the game's theme, and the angel supplies expertise without taking control."},{"t":"Take the bank loan, to keep 100% ownership.","fb":"With no income yet, fixed repayments at 10% are very risky."},{"t":"Rely only on the grant, to avoid giving away any ownership.","fb":"USD 15,000 cannot fund regional expansion, and grants are competitive and slow to arrive."}]}
