     "up": {"title":"Funding methods tick table: which method fits? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p class=\"credit\"><i>From the Funding Models exercise</i></p><p>Harder features this time, with close options: angels and venture capital, accelerators and incubators, grants and competition prizes. Choose the method each feature matches BEST, then try the full tick table.</p><div class=\"row\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"btn gold\" data-go=\"edpmgames\" data-k=\"fundingtick\">Open the full Funding Methods Tick Table</button></div>","items":[{"text":"An individual invests early, often with personal mentoring, usually for a smaller sum than a fund would.","options":["Angel investor","Venture capital","Loan","Accelerator"],"answer":0,"fb":"An individual investing personal money early is an angel. Venture capital comes from a firm with pooled funds."},{"text":"A short, fixed-length programme with seed money, mentoring and a demo day, usually for a small equity stake.","options":["Angel investor","Incubator","Accelerator","Grant"],"answer":2,"fb":"Short and intensive with a demo day: an accelerator. Incubators are longer and support earlier ideas."},{"text":"The creator receives nothing unless the funding goal is reached.","options":["All-or-nothing crowdfunding","Pre-sales","Donation-based crowdfunding","Sponsorship"],"answer":0,"fb":"All-or-nothing platforms pay out only when the goal is met."},{"text":"Proves demand by selling the finished product before it is made.","options":["Donation-based crowdfunding","Pre-sales","Grant","Subscriptions"],"answer":1,"fb":"Selling before the product exists is pre-sales."},{"text":"A partner funds or distributes the project in return for a percentage of future income, but takes no ownership.","options":["Loan","Sponsorship","Revenue sharing","Equity financing"],"answer":2,"fb":"A share of income without ownership is revenue sharing."},{"text":"Must be repaid on a schedule even if the project earns nothing, but the founders keep all of the business.","options":["Venture capital","Grant","Revenue sharing","Loan"],"answer":3,"fb":"Scheduled repayment and full ownership: a loan."},{"text":"Large sums for businesses that can scale fast, usually with board seats and growth targets.","options":["Angel investor","Accelerator","Venture capital","Bootstrapping"],"answer":2,"fb":"Venture capital firms invest large pooled sums and expect fast growth and influence."},{"text":"Full creative control, but the project grows only as fast as the founder's savings and early sales allow.","options":["Sponsorship","Crowdfunding","Bootstrapping","Grant"],"answer":2,"fb":"Self-funding is bootstrapping."},{"text":"Money for a defined purpose, won through a competitive written proposal and followed by a report.","options":["Grant","Donation","Competition prize","Sponsorship"],"answer":0,"fb":"Proposal plus reporting points to a grant. A competition prize is won in a contest, usually without a spending report."}],"win":"<p>Excellent. You separated methods that share features. Now try the full tick table, where you tick EVERY method that fits each feature.</p><div class=\"row\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"btn gold\" data-go=\"edpmgames\" data-k=\"fundingtick\">Open the full Funding Methods Tick Table</button></div>"}
