     "type": "scenario",
     "game": true,
     "title": "Fund the Soca Stories podcast",
     "intro": "<p>You are launching the podcast Soca Stories, interviewing veteran soca artists across the Eastern Caribbean. You need about USD 6,000 for microphones, travel and editing. Choose your funding mix.</p>",
     "nodes": {
      "start": {
       "text": "<p>You have no income yet and no assets. A bank offers a USD 6,000 loan at high interest, repayable from next month. A national cultural fund is accepting grant proposals for heritage projects. Which do you pursue first?</p>",
       "choices": [
        {
         "t": "Write a strong proposal for the cultural fund grant.",
         "to": "n2",
         "fb": "Good. A heritage project fits the fund's objectives, and grants do not need repaying."
        },
        {
         "t": "Take the full bank loan now.",
         "to": "bad1",
         "fb": "Debt with no income means repayments you cannot meet."
        }
       ]
      },
      "n2": {
       "text": "<p>The fund awards USD 3,000. You have 1,500 loyal followers from your interview clips. How do you raise more?</p>",
       "choices": [
        {
         "t": "Launch a crowdfunding campaign with rewards such as early episodes and signed posters.",
         "to": "n3",
         "fb": "Crowdfunding raises money directly from your community."
        },
        {
         "t": "Sell 40% of the podcast to the first investor who asks.",
         "to": "bad2",
         "fb": "Giving away so much equity this early, for a small sum, loses control of your project."
        }
       ]
      },
      "n3": {
       "text": "<p>The podcast launches and grows to 10,000 monthly listeners. How do you sustain it?</p>",
       "choices": [
        {
         "t": "Combine podcast ad insertion, a paid membership with bonus episodes and a brand partnership with a regional airline.",
         "to": "good",
         "fb": "A mix of income models spreads risk."
        },
        {
         "t": "Rely entirely on one platform's payments.",
         "to": "bad3",
         "fb": "Depending on one platform creates disruption risk."
        }
       ]
      },
      "good": {
       "text": "<p><b>Success!</b> Your grant, crowdfund and income mix cover the costs, you keep full ownership, and no single change can sink the show. You chose funding that fitted each stage of the project.</p>",
       "end": "good"
      },
      "bad1": {
       "text": "<p><b>In debt.</b> Repayments start before the first episode is released. Try again: with no income, avoid debt.</p>",
       "end": "bad"
      },
      "bad2": {
       "text": "<p><b>Control lost.</b> The investor now decides which artists you interview. Try again.</p>",
       "end": "bad"
      },
      "bad3": {
       "text": "<p><b>Income collapses.</b> The platform changes its terms and your earnings fall by 70%. Try again and diversify.</p>",
       "end": "bad"
      }
     },
