     "up": {"title":"Fund the Soca Stories podcast (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","intro":"<p>You are launching Soca Stories, interviewing veteran soca artists across the Eastern Caribbean. You need USD 6,000. This time every source has conditions, so read the terms before you choose.</p>","nodes":{"start":{"text":"<p>You have no income and no assets. Offers: a bank loan of USD 6,000 at 12%, repayable from next month; a national cultural fund offering up to USD 3,000, with a proposal and budget due in six weeks; and an investor offering USD 6,000 for 40% of the podcast.</p>","choices":[{"t":"Take the loan and repay it from future advertising.","to":"bad2","fb":"With no income, repayments start before any advertising exists."},{"t":"Write a detailed proposal and budget for the cultural fund, and plan a crowdfunding campaign to raise the rest.","to":"n2","fb":"Good. Free money that fits a heritage project, plus a route to the balance that builds your audience."},{"t":"Take the investor's USD 6,000 for 40% so you can start immediately.","to":"bad1","fb":"Speed is tempting, but 40% for a small sum gives away a large share of control at the start."}]},"n2":{"text":"<p>The fund awards USD 3,000, to be spent only on production costs and reported with receipts. You still need USD 3,000 for travel and marketing. You have 1,500 loyal followers.</p>","choices":[{"t":"Run an all-or-nothing crowdfunding campaign with a realistic USD 3,000 goal, rewards you can afford to deliver, and a launch video of interview clips.","to":"n3","fb":"A realistic goal suits your audience size, and affordable rewards protect your budget."},{"t":"Spend the grant on marketing, because marketing is more urgent.","to":"bad4","fb":"Grants must be spent as agreed. Breaking the conditions risks repayment and your reputation with the fund."},{"t":"Set a USD 10,000 all-or-nothing goal to be safe.","to":"bad3","fb":"An unrealistic goal on an all-or-nothing platform risks getting nothing."}]},"n3":{"text":"<p>Six months later you have 10,000 monthly listeners. A regional airline offers sponsorship, but its first draft contract lets it approve every episode before release.</p>","choices":[{"t":"Accept the airline's terms in full.","to":"ok1","fb":"Income now, but the sponsor controls your content."},{"t":"Accept sponsorship that includes the airline's adverts and logo, but negotiate a clause that keeps editorial control with you.","to":"n4","fb":"You gained income and protected your independence in writing."}]},"n4":{"text":"<p>How will you keep Soca Stories going for the long term?</p>","choices":[{"t":"Combine podcast ad insertion, a paid membership with bonus interviews, the airline sponsorship and licensing of archive interviews to a regional broadcaster.","to":"good","fb":"A mix of platform-controlled and creator-controlled income spreads the risk."},{"t":"Rely entirely on one platform's advertising payments.","to":"bad5","fb":"One income stream controlled by one platform creates disruption risk."}]},"good":{"text":"<p><b>Grade One funding plan!</b> A grant for production, crowdfunding for travel and marketing, a sponsor on fair terms and four income streams. You kept full ownership and editorial control, and no single change can sink the show.</p>","end":"good"},"ok1":{"text":"<p><b>Funded but not free.</b> The airline asks you to drop an interview critical of tourism policy. Lesson: read and negotiate sponsorship terms.</p>","end":"ok"},"bad1":{"text":"<p><b>Control lost.</b> The investor now decides which artists you interview. Lesson: avoid giving away large stakes early for small sums.</p>","end":"bad"},"bad2":{"text":"<p><b>In debt.</b> Repayments start before the first episode is released. Lesson: with no income, avoid debt.</p>","end":"bad"},"bad3":{"text":"<p><b>Nothing raised.</b> You reach USD 4,100 of USD 10,000, so the platform pays out nothing. Lesson: set an all-or-nothing goal you can actually reach.</p>","end":"bad"},"bad4":{"text":"<p><b>Grant recalled.</b> Your report does not match the agreed budget and the fund asks for its money back. Lesson: grants come with conditions.</p>","end":"bad"},"bad5":{"text":"<p><b>Income collapses.</b> The platform changes its terms and your earnings fall by 70%. Lesson: diversify.</p>","end":"bad"}}}
