     "up": {"title":"Agile or waterfall? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>These behaviours are less obvious. Some agile practices involve careful planning, and some waterfall practices sound sensible. Sort each one by the approach it reflects.</p>","main":"Is this typical of agile or waterfall project management?","bins":["Agile","Waterfall"],"items":[{"t":"Script, shoot, edit and delivery must each be fully finished before the next begins.","bin":1,"fb":"One stage after another is the waterfall sequence."},{"t":"The client signs off a complete specification, and any change needs a formal request and an extra fee.","bin":1,"fb":"Resisting late change is waterfall."},{"t":"Actual spending is compared with the budget after every two-week cycle and money is reallocated.","bin":0,"fb":"Budget review in every cycle is part of the agile model."},{"t":"The team delivers one large release at the very end of the project.","bin":1,"fb":"A single final delivery is waterfall."},{"t":"The team builds a minimum viable version of the app and tests it with 20 users before adding features.","bin":0,"fb":"Testing a simple version early is agile."},{"t":"Testing happens only after all the content is complete.","bin":1,"fb":"Late testing is typical of waterfall."},{"t":"Feedback from a test audience changes the order of the episodes still to be made.","bin":0,"fb":"Reprioritising the backlog after review is agile."},{"t":"The scope states what is excluded, but backlog priorities are reordered every cycle.","bin":0,"fb":"Agile still sets scope; it stays flexible on priorities."},{"t":"A detailed chart fixes every task date for six months, and the manager's job is to keep to it.","bin":1,"fb":"A fixed, linear schedule is waterfall."},{"t":"A retrospective after each cycle changes how the team runs its stand-ups.","bin":0,"fb":"Improving the process every cycle is agile."}],"win":"Excellent. You saw that agile still plans, but plans in cycles, while waterfall fixes the plan and delivers once."}
