     "up": {"title":"Build a winning pitch (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>Eight lines from the pitch for \"SKN Eats Local\", with the element names removed. Put them in the order of a winning pitch.</p>","blocks":[{"t":"\"Imagine stepping off the ship and eating where the locals eat, on your very first day.\""},{"t":"\"Most visitors never find the island's roadside vendors and lolos.\""},{"t":"\"Our app shows every local vendor near you, with today's specials.\""},{"t":"\"Over a million cruise visitors arrive each year, and mobile ordering is growing right now.\""},{"t":"\"In our pilot month, 40 vendors joined and 1,200 people downloaded the app.\""},{"t":"\"Review sites list restaurants, but not roadside vendors.\""},{"t":"\"Our developer has built two school apps; our marketer runs a page with 10,000 followers.\""},{"t":"\"We ask for USD 8,000. The app is free for users, USD 15 a month for vendors, available in app stores and at the pier, and promoted by local creators.\""}],"win":"Correct. Vision, problem, solution, market and why now, traction, competition, team, and finally the ask with the 4Ps."}
